{"name":"Heirloom Apricot","hex":"#f4bea6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heirloom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A valued possession that has been passed down through the generations.","An old crop variety that has been passed down through generations of farmers by seed saving and cultivation, in contrast to modern cultivars used in large-scale agriculture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heirloom"},{"term":"apricot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round sweet and juicy stone fruit, resembling peach or plum in taste, with a yellow-orange flesh, lightly fuzzy skin and a large seed inside.","The apricot tree, Prunus armeniaca."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-orange colour, like that of an apricot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apricot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heirloom","blocks":[{"text":"In popular usage, an heirloom is something that has been passed down for generations through family members. Examples are a family Bible, antiques, weapons or jewellery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Soldier%27s_return.jpg/330px-Soldier%27s_return.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heirloom","wikidata":"Q16842191"},{"title":"Apricot","blocks":[{"text":"An apricot is a fruit, or the tree that bears the fruit, of several species in the genus Prunus. Usually an apricot is from the species Prunus armeniaca, but the fruits of the other species in Prunus sect. Armeniaca are also called apricots. In 2023, world production of apricots was 3.7 million tonnes, led by Turkey with 20% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot","wikidata":"Q3733836"},{"title":"Apricot (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Apricot is a light yellowish-orangish color that is similar to the color of apricots. However, it is paler than actual apricots."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot_(color)","wikidata":"Q1324818"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg/500px-Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg/1280px-Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg/500px-Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Heirloom 1893 pocket watch with 18 carat gold case","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWatch%2C_pocket_(AM_1985.79-2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Turkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg/250px-Turkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Turkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg/500px-Turkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Turkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg/250px-Turkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATurkey.Pasa_Baglari005.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Healthy_leaves_of_apricot_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Healthy_leaves_of_apricot_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wiki